<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="5">

  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="9 3/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BROOKE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No">
              <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style=""></Text>
            </Paragraph>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JORDAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No">
              <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style=""></Text>
            </Paragraph>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Bruce Peninsula National Park</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style=""></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The stage is a sunny nature trail. Its edge is an escarpment.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Jordan</Text>
      <Text> enters, holding a map. They hike upstage.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Brooke</Text>
      <Text> exhaustedly trails </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Jordan</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The devil is in the details.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Hell yeah, this map sure is full of devils. Sweat it out. It’s good that you’re hydrated.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yes. I wasn’t the last time I was here.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The park’s sixty square miles. Was it near this spot where it all went</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic"> down</Text>
      <Text>? Where’s the cliff?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I don’t recall much of Bruce Peninsula at all, but the press does remember I almost went </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">down</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>What you </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">did</Text>
      <Text> risking your life is no pressing matter. What you’ll </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">do</Text>
      <Text> with your life will press on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Sure. So, any news coming out of New York?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Nothing much. Actually, Savanna finished kindergarten with career day where I showed her class the things I do with my life.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Get them while they’re young! Are you out there getting kids interested in physiology?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Her gym teacher barely gets them to do jumping jacks. Getting kids to understand their bodies is a bit of a stretch. Did you stretch at all?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Don’t ask.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Well, we’ll get our answer. Come on, we have a ways to go.</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps"></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Jordan</Text>
      <Text> and </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Brooke</Text>
      <Text> hike about.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You know, Brooke, we could’ve hiked somewhere cool. Like a volcano.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Oh here we go again...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Remember that video of Savanna’s teacher and a model volcano, and the joy on my kid’s face. You’d be her hero if you got into volcanoes!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Savanna’s not into sand dunes? When she reaches high school, share my papers with her in the American Geophysical Union Advances.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Your love of sand will always be unexplainable.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BROOKE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You two can visit one. There’s... I don’t know New York ones on the top of my head.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’ve visited some. You heard of Fire Island?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That’s how my legs feel right now. On fire.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You should’ve stretched. Everything stretches. Animals, plants, land... I’m sure rocks do. Does the Earth stretch their layers?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Their crust constantly stretches with tectonic tension. Like our conversation and this hike!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style=""></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s your </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">fault</Text>
      <Text> you’re the best geomorphologist I know. A leg up for the coolest job title.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.25" RightIndent="7.25" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="General">
      <DualDialogue>
        <SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
          <IgnoredRanges/>
          <IgnoredWords/>
        </SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Brooke</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>Thanks?</Text>
          <Text></Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Jordan</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>But nothing quite as </Text>
          <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">hot</Text>
          <Text> as a volcanologist’s.</Text>
        </Paragraph>
      </DualDialogue>
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Most volcanologists end up not on the field but in the labs which are air-conditioned.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>We have a ways to go in conditioning you to feel light as air like nothing else matters.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Jordan</Text>
      <Text> and </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Brooke</Text>
      <Text> stay put.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Things have been heavy lately.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Jordan. You can tell me anything.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s my body...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.25" RightIndent="7.25" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="General">
      <DualDialogue>
        <SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
          <IgnoredRanges/>
          <IgnoredWords/>
        </SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Brooke</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>Did you have a bad doctor’s appointment?</Text>
          <Text></Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Jordan</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>I’m regaining weight.</Text>
        </Paragraph>
      </DualDialogue>
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Your old body’s coming back? Congrats!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Stop. I’m getting bad eyeballs online.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Look, we’ll go on more hikes together. It’s good to lay off social media every so often. Ignore those negative comments. The internet has unhealthy body standards.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yeah, I don’t wanna see another post about your mocktails with your </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">weirdass</Text>
      <Text> partner.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I need to be with my Celestine, the finest </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">Astronomy on Tap </Text>
      <Text>host. Plus, there’s nothing to do in </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">UrbanBeat</Text>
      <Text> or Lansing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Does Lansing host a marathon?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The River Run I think is half. There are full ones throughout Michigan, like Grand Rapids.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You should be used to this sorta landscape. It’s virtually the same Great Lakes climate.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Sure, Pleistocene glaciers carved lands we walk on. I appreciate our great bodies of water, much like how you should appreciate your body-</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Humanity has a ways to go when it comes to carving trails for themselves...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="4.00" RightIndent="7.38" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="Yes" Type="Action">
      <Text>The clouds engulf the Sun.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Hopefully, it doesn’t start downpouring.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The world’s sweating. Rain is good for us all.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Based on the </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">NIH</Text>
      <Text>, obesity is prevalent in places with dark or overcast weather patterns.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You were a rock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.25" RightIndent="7.25" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="General">
      <DualDialogue>
        <SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
          <IgnoredRanges/>
          <IgnoredWords/>
        </SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Jordan</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>I weighed as much as he does.</Text>
          <Text></Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Brooke</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">A porous rock</Text>
          <Text>.</Text>
        </Paragraph>
      </DualDialogue>
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.25" RightIndent="7.25" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="General">
      <DualDialogue>
        <SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
          <IgnoredRanges/>
          <IgnoredWords/>
        </SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Jordan</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>He’s most certainly a billionaire by now.</Text>
          <Text></Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Brooke</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>No. You were like a sandstone.</Text>
        </Paragraph>
      </DualDialogue>
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.25" RightIndent="7.25" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="General">
      <DualDialogue>
        <SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
          <IgnoredRanges/>
          <IgnoredWords/>
        </SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Jordan</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>Ya head’s in the sand again!</Text>
          <Text></Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Brooke</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">Pumice then</Text>
          <Text>. Volcanic rocks.</Text>
        </Paragraph>
      </DualDialogue>
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style=""></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Immense porosity- For these holes inside you, you filled it with matrices containing clay and micas. They were what held you, an unconfined aquifer, together, but all you saw was this groundwater you’re holding-</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.25" RightIndent="7.25" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="General">
      <DualDialogue>
        <SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
          <IgnoredRanges/>
          <IgnoredWords/>
        </SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Jordan</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>Ugh, water weight.</Text>
          <Text></Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Brooke</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>You said hydration was good!</Text>
        </Paragraph>
      </DualDialogue>
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And now you’re losing yourself.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.25" RightIndent="7.25" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="General">
      <DualDialogue>
        <SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
          <IgnoredRanges/>
          <IgnoredWords/>
        </SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Jordan</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>I’m not anorexic. </Text>
          <Text></Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Brooke</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>I’m saying you’ve changed.</Text>
        </Paragraph>
      </DualDialogue>
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">I’ll speak your language as a former rock</Text>
      <Text>. I am </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">permeable</Text>
      <Text>? So water moves in and out of me. They take away my old features and fresh water grants me new details. Same is done in other natural systems. Matrices in eukaryotic cells. During cytokinesis, they clone... </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">Oh</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">So cells stay identical and keep their details</Text>
      <Text>?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JOrdan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Forget it. I lost track of my thoughts much like we lost track of where we’re going. This map is Hell. We have no ways to go!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="4.00" RightIndent="7.38" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="Yes" Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Jordan</Text>
      <Text> crumples the map, then almost puts it in their mouth before tossing it away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>This hike was for </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">your</Text>
      <Text> sake!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m grateful. But I have thick skin. I got to.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JORDAn</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You are as superficial as the stratum corneum. The surface layer of the </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">epidermis</Text>
      <Text>. Hey, that’d be a good name for a boat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Your body is so foreboding.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>My life is healthy and balanced. I drink tons of water. And my family is proud of the physiologist I grew up to be.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.25" RightIndent="7.25" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="General">
      <DualDialogue>
        <SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
          <IgnoredRanges/>
          <IgnoredWords/>
        </SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Brooke</Text>
          <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style=""></Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>Your judgmental family holds no water. Savanna is fine.</Text>
          <Text></Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Jordan</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>They are not judgmental!</Text>
        </Paragraph>
      </DualDialogue>
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style=""></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Balance is like groundwater. There is a zone of aeration and saturation. Air is running in your pores and water is running out of them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>My skin has so much room to breathe that it feels the breeze. </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Brrr...</Text>
      <Text> My mind is at ease.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Then you wouldn’t mind telling me why your body has been in uncanny valley.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Uncanny?! You knew my goal has been to get slim since we left Northern. Michigan is the space to focus on schooling, but I can achieve anything in New York. I’ve been in very open-minded circles who know what’s best for their bodies while I had Savanna.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You got fake friends who make your degree go to waste.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You got a ways to go when it comes to making friends.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Brooke</Text>
      <Text> picks up the crumpled map. They contort it based on their cycle of erosion talk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>What are you staging?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BrookE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Your intervention. There are three stages in the stream cycle of erosion: youth, maturity, and old age.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Your field sure is analogous to our life cycle.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Geomorphologists do all we can to be relatable. Can you categorize these valleys in this map?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I see the narrow wrinkle as youth, the widest is old age, and in-betweens are like mature.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Spot on. The youth stage has irregular steep gradients, no floodplains, and goes through downcutting by eroding the riverbed. It gives some valleys a V shape. Maturity has smooth gradients, few waterfalls, and meanders. These valleys are all about U, U-shaped. And old age is the extreme, broader maturity stage.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Speaking of analogy: Letting go of minor things get easier with time cause your valley’s wider. My body’s “uncanny.” Who cares? We are almost in the maturity cycle. It’s all about you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I need to point out that each geologist discerns stream cycles differently. Each stage is necessarily transitional into the next, so there are some degree of overlap in landform characteristics which is to be expected.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s like going from childhood to adolescence. It’s different for everybody! Even valleys have liminal spaces.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>“Liminal?”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Whenever my yoga instructor gets her ways to go, she has us repeat...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Jordan</Text>
      <Text> meditates. </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Brooke</Text>
      <Text> follows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JORDAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>“A place where who we were ends and who we are begins.”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And I’m here. Returning to the cliff that should have been my end...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The motorcycle accident did end </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">you</Text>
      <Text> but only the bad parts of you. Parts of your quartz.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Granite?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Granted, I got into jewelry ever since my chubby fingers can fit a five and a half.
</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="8" Style="">
</Text>      <Text>Alright, this five-and-a-half hour self-deprecating ends here. Let’s get a move on.</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps"></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.25" RightIndent="7.25" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="General">
      <DualDialogue>
        <SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
          <IgnoredRanges/>
          <IgnoredWords/>
        </SpellCheckIgnoreLists>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Brooke</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>So glad you’ve move on, </Text>
          <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">in the wrong direction</Text>
          <Text>. </Text>
          <Text></Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Character">
          <Text>Jordan</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
          <Text>Glad you now see it that way-
My path is righteous!</Text>
        </Paragraph>
      </DualDialogue>
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style=""></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>This whole trail starts at Niagara Falls?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Five hundred miles. What you scientists say...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And Canadians here: eight hundred kilometers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>What else did Canada get wrong? The drinking age at eighteen years. It should be 118.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You’re leaving me heated. Cut it out, Jordan!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Alcohol interferes with our brain's pathways to communicate, leaving us with no empathy, like a massasauga rattlesnake we bumped into earlier.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I shouldn’t have been drinking poison at that age. Or cross the Ambassador Bridge into this country to get booze and party. I’m a V!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Sweat it all out. You have less of a ways to go-</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Brooke</Text>
      <Text> runs away from </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Jordan</Text>
      <Text>. </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Brooke</Text>
      <Text> eventually finds the edge of the stage, where they sit.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Brooke! I’m sorry to open up old wounds! These are minor things. Dumb things you done as a minor. We’ve all done dumb things. You just got to release that water weight.
</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="8" Style="">
</Text>      <Text>Brooke! Speaking like a rock: You’re still a youthful stream cycle. Rigid gradient valley. You need to let the river rock your sides until it carves your valley into the shape of U.
</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="8" Style="">
</Text>      <Text>Brooke. I admit I am rougher around the edges. I know you hoped I’d be the mature stream cycle. Yeah... Now I live in New York City, conflating self-respect with something else.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="8" Style=""></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Brooke. You mean the world since Marquette. The body of the overweight freshman is gone, but my heart’s still here. It’s getting dark. Leaving me alone out here is so thin-skinned of you!
</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="8" Style="">
</Text>      <Text>Brooke... I am getting thin-skinned. Even if I’m hydrated, I’m a rock with waterless pores. What you called: aeration. Maybe, I should go reexamine my health and gain the few pounds.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m surprised you haven’t tried calling! Well, I’m proud you’ve got your mind off the phone for once in a long time. Aside from that, you’re still full of hot air. Sweat that out!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="8" Style=""></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Brooke... You know what...
</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="8" Style="">
</Text>      <Text>Savanna is getting into astronomy, so we should head to the beach sometime with you and Celestine and introduce Savanna to some sand dunes before stargazing then! How’s that sound?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You are out of this world... Fine. I’ll stop burying my head in the sand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Where are you?!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m not too far. Come! You’ll enjoy the look of this body of water.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Before I ever do, I have a ways to go...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="4.00" RightIndent="7.38" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="Yes" Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Jordan</Text>
      <Text> reaches the escarpment. They sit with </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Brooke</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Niagara Escarpment seems past old age stage.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>At least three thousand years ago.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Are you getting past your high school phase?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Three thousand days ago...? Well, me and the other seniors had the time of our lives here. A few drinks. </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Italic">A lot to drink</Text>
      <Text>. Key in the ignition switch. My pop’s motorcycle plummeting off this cliff. That one tree stopping me. Stupid teen-</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And yet, you had a future ahead and didn’t die-</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style=""></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The Bruce Peninsula Press contacted my school. General Motors Foundation took my engineering scholarship. And that humiliating graduation, almost non-graduation.</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps"></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Anything beyond such minor details?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style=""></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Nothing major.
</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="8" Style="">
</Text>      <Text>I changed majors at our college that wasn’t my choice. It took years before I returned to the beach; for my geology elective. Now I work for the Alliance for the Great Lakes. You happy?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JOrdan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You’re sweating the big things!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I try to remind myself that there are bigger issues than irresponsible kids. Last time, there was a dune complex below. Lake Huron probably swallowed it. Earth is sweating... Anyways, it’s a worry for everyday after today.
</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="8" Style="">
</Text>      <Text>I still have a ways to go, Jordan. The memories erode me. But, I know over time things I did as a high schooler are less likely to kick up a storm.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Way to go, Brooke.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The clouds sweat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Jordan</Text>
      <Text> and </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Brooke </Text>
      <Text>are in major perspiration.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JORDAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But before we hike back, Mother Nature can be a bit of a stretch...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Do ask.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Jordan</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Can you answer for the waves below?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Brooke</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Things from a minor wind to a major earthquake can help “Mother Nature” make waves. And years of weathering them made this the escarpment that they are. The devil is in their details.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="End of Act">
      <Text>End of Play</Text>
    </Paragraph>
  </Content>

